q q BT 9 TL/F1 7.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 227.9553 25.51181 Tm (Script-Controlled ACL | )Tj[-4112.0007]TJ ( | Page 4)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 765.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 19 TL/F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (1. INTRODUCTION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 741.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (1.1 Project Overview)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 679.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 46.5 Tm (The Script-Controlled ACL project is designed to implement fine-grained record access control based on a field)Tj T* (value. An ACL is a rule that determines whether a user or group is allowed to perform an operation on a protected)Tj T* (resource. In this project, the authorization decision is not based only on who the user is; it also considers)Tj T* (information stored in the requested record.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 616.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 46.5 Tm (For example, a policy can permit a user to read records whose department field matches the user's department,)Tj T* (while denying records belonging to other departments. Similar rules can be created for ownership, project code,)Tj T* (region, classification, status, or another business field. The script evaluates the condition before the requested)Tj T* (record is exposed.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 567.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm (The proposed workflow is: authenticate the user )Tj/F3 9.5 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( identify the requested record )Tj/F3 9.5 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( read the relevant field )Tj/F3 9.5 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.5 Tf T* (evaluate the ACL script )Tj/F3 9.5 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( grant or deny access )Tj/F3 9.5 Tf <ae>Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( log the decision. This creates a clear authorization boundary)Tj T* (and makes the policy easier to adapt when business rules change.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 544.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (High-Level Workflow)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.02362 501.8661 cm .956863 .968627 .980392 rg 0 38 493.2283 -38 re f